   7:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   * @brief   This file provides firmware functions to manage the following 
   8:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   *          functionalities of the Real-Time Clock (RTC) peripheral:
   9:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   *           + Initialization
  10:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   *           + Calendar (Time and Date) configuration
  11:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   *           + Alarms (Alarm A and Alarm B) configuration
  12:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   *           + WakeUp Timer configuration
  13:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   *           + Daylight Saving configuration
  14:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   *           + Output pin Configuration
  15:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   *           + Coarse digital Calibration configuration
  16:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   *           + Smooth digital Calibration configuration
  17:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   *           + TimeStamp configuration
  18:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   *           + Tampers configuration
  19:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   *           + Backup Data Registers configuration
  20:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   *           + Shift control synchronisation    
  21:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   *           + RTC Tamper and TimeStamp Pins Selection and Output Type Config configuration
  22:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   *           + Interrupts and flags management
  23:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   *
  24:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c **** @verbatim
  25:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c **** 
  26:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  ===================================================================
  27:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****               ##### Backup Domain Operating Condition #####
  28:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  ===================================================================
  29:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  [..] The real-time clock (RTC), the RTC backup registers, and the backup 
  30:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****       SRAM (BKP SRAM) can be powered from the VBAT voltage when the main 
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccgzaD3d.s 			page 2


  31:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****       VDD supply is powered off.
  32:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****       To retain the content of the RTC backup registers, backup SRAM, and supply 
  33:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****       the RTC when VDD is turned off, VBAT pin can be connected to an optional 
  34:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****       standby voltage supplied by a battery or by another source.
  35:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c **** 
  36:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  [..] To allow the RTC to operate even when the main digital supply (VDD) is turned
  37:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****       off, the VBAT pin powers the following blocks:
  38:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (#) The RTC
  39:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (#) The LSE oscillator
  40:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (#) The backup SRAM when the low power backup regulator is enabled
  41:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (#) PC13 to PC15 I/Os, plus PI8 I/O (when available)
  42:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   
  43:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  [..] When the backup domain is supplied by VDD (analog switch connected to VDD),
  44:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****       the following functions are available:
  45:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (#) PC14 and PC15 can be used as either GPIO or LSE pins
  46:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (#) PC13 can be used as a GPIO or as the RTC_AF1 pin
  47:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (#) PI8 can be used as a GPIO or as the RTC_AF2 pin
  48:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   
  49:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  [..] When the backup domain is supplied by VBAT (analog switch connected to VBAT 
  50:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****       because VDD is not present), the following functions are available:
  51:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (#) PC14 and PC15 can be used as LSE pins only
  52:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (#) PC13 can be used as the RTC_AF1 pin 
  53:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (#) PI8 can be used as the RTC_AF2 pin
  54:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   
  55:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****             
  56:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****                    ##### Backup Domain Reset #####
  57:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  ===================================================================
  58:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  [..] The backup domain reset sets all RTC registers and the RCC_BDCR register 
  59:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****       to their reset values. The BKPSRAM is not affected by this reset. The only
  60:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****       way of resetting the BKPSRAM is through the Flash interface by requesting 
  61:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****       a protection level change from 1 to 0.
  62:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  [..] A backup domain reset is generated when one of the following events occurs:
  63:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (#) Software reset, triggered by setting the BDRST bit in the 
  64:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        RCC Backup domain control register (RCC_BDCR). You can use the
  65:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        RCC_BackupResetCmd().
  66:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (#) VDD or VBAT power on, if both supplies have previously been powered off.
  67:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   
  68:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c **** 
  69:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****                    ##### Backup Domain Access #####
  70:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  ===================================================================
  71:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  [..] After reset, the backup domain (RTC registers, RTC backup data 
  72:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****       registers and backup SRAM) is protected against possible unwanted write 
  73:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****       accesses. 
  74:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  [..] To enable access to the RTC Domain and RTC registers, proceed as follows:
  75:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) Enable the Power Controller (PWR) APB1 interface clock using the
  76:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        RCC_APB1PeriphClockCmd() function.
  77:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) Enable access to RTC domain using the PWR_BackupAccessCmd() function.
  78:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) Select the RTC clock source using the RCC_RTCCLKConfig() function.
  79:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) Enable RTC Clock using the RCC_RTCCLKCmd() function.
  80:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   
  81:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   
  82:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****                   ##### How to use RTC Driver #####
  83:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  ===================================================================
  84:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  [..] 
  85:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) Enable the RTC domain access (see description in the section above)
  86:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) Configure the RTC Prescaler (Asynchronous and Synchronous) and RTC hour 
  87:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        format using the RTC_Init() function.
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccgzaD3d.s 			page 3


  88:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   
  89:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  *** Time and Date configuration ***
  90:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  ===================================
  91:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  [..] 
  92:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) To configure the RTC Calendar (Time and Date) use the RTC_SetTime()
  93:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        and RTC_SetDate() functions.
  94:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) To read the RTC Calendar, use the RTC_GetTime() and RTC_GetDate() functions.
  95:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) Use the RTC_DayLightSavingConfig() function to add or sub one
  96:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        hour to the RTC Calendar.    
  97:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   
  98:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  *** Alarm configuration ***
  99:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  ===========================
 100:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  [..]
 101:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) To configure the RTC Alarm use the RTC_SetAlarm() function.
 102:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) Enable the selected RTC Alarm using the RTC_AlarmCmd() function
 103:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) To read the RTC Alarm, use the RTC_GetAlarm() function.
 104:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) To read the RTC alarm SubSecond, use the RTC_GetAlarmSubSecond() function.
 105:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   
 106:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  *** RTC Wakeup configuration ***
 107:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  ================================
 108:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  [..] 
 109:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) Configure the RTC Wakeup Clock source use the RTC_WakeUpClockConfig()
 110:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        function.
 111:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) Configure the RTC WakeUp Counter using the RTC_SetWakeUpCounter() function  
 112:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) Enable the RTC WakeUp using the RTC_WakeUpCmd() function  
 113:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) To read the RTC WakeUp Counter register, use the RTC_GetWakeUpCounter() 
 114:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        function.
 115:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   
 116:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  *** Outputs configuration ***
 117:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  =============================
 118:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  [..] The RTC has 2 different outputs:
 119:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) AFO_ALARM: this output is used to manage the RTC Alarm A, Alarm B
 120:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        and WaKeUp signals. To output the selected RTC signal on RTC_AF1 pin, use the 
 121:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        RTC_OutputConfig() function.                
 122:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) AFO_CALIB: this output is 512Hz signal or 1Hz. To output the RTC Clock on 
 123:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        RTC_AF1 pin, use the RTC_CalibOutputCmd() function.
 124:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   
 125:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  *** Smooth digital Calibration configuration ***
 126:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  ================================================    
 127:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  [..]
 128:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) Configure the RTC Original Digital Calibration Value and the corresponding
 129:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        calibration cycle period (32s,16s and 8s) using the RTC_SmoothCalibConfig() 
 130:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        function.
 131:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   
 132:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  *** Coarse digital Calibration configuration ***
 133:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  ================================================
 134:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  [..]
 135:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) Configure the RTC Coarse Calibration Value and the corresponding
 136:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        sign using the RTC_CoarseCalibConfig() function.
 137:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) Enable the RTC Coarse Calibration using the RTC_CoarseCalibCmd() function  
 138:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   
 139:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  *** TimeStamp configuration ***
 140:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  ===============================
 141:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  [..]
 142:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) Configure the RTC_AF1 trigger and enables the RTC TimeStamp using the RTC
 143:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****       _TimeStampCmd() function.
 144:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) To read the RTC TimeStamp Time and Date register, use the RTC_GetTimeStamp()
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccgzaD3d.s 			page 4


 145:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        function.
 146:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) To read the RTC TimeStamp SubSecond register, use the 
 147:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        RTC_GetTimeStampSubSecond() function.
 148:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) The TAMPER1 alternate function can be mapped either to RTC_AF1(PC13)
 149:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        or RTC_AF2 (PI8) depending on the value of TAMP1INSEL bit in 
 150:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        RTC_TAFCR register. You can use the  RTC_TamperPinSelection() function to
 151:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        select the corresponding pin.     
 152:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   
 153:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  *** Tamper configuration ***
 154:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  ============================
 155:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  [..]
 156:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) Enable the RTC Tamper using the RTC_TamperCmd() function.
 157:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) Configure the Tamper filter count using RTC_TamperFilterConfig()
 158:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        function. 
 159:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) Configure the RTC Tamper trigger Edge or Level according to the Tamper 
 160:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        filter (if equal to 0 Edge else Level) value using the RTC_TamperConfig() 
 161:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        function.
 162:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) Configure the Tamper sampling frequency using RTC_TamperSamplingFreqConfig()
 163:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        function.
 164:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) Configure the Tamper precharge or discharge duration using 
 165:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        RTC_TamperPinsPrechargeDuration() function.
 166:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) Enable the Tamper Pull-UP using RTC_TamperPullUpDisableCmd() function.
 167:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) Enable the Time stamp on Tamper detection event using  
 168:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        TC_TSOnTamperDetecCmd() function.
 169:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) The TIMESTAMP alternate function can be mapped to either RTC_AF1 
 170:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        or RTC_AF2 depending on the value of the TSINSEL bit in the RTC_TAFCR 
 171:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        register. You can use the  RTC_TimeStampPinSelection() function to select 
 172:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        the corresponding pin. 
 173:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   
 174:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  *** Backup Data Registers configuration ***
 175:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  ===========================================
 176:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  [..]
 177:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) To write to the RTC Backup Data registers, use the RTC_WriteBackupRegister()
 178:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        function.  
 179:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) To read the RTC Backup Data registers, use the RTC_ReadBackupRegister()
 180:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****        function.
 181:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    
 182:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c **** 
 183:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****                   ##### RTC and low power modes #####
 184:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  ===================================================================
 185:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  [..] The MCU can be woken up from a low power mode by an RTC alternate 
 186:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****       function.
 187:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  [..] The RTC alternate functions are the RTC alarms (Alarm A and Alarm B), 
 188:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****       RTC wakeup, RTC tamper event detection and RTC time stamp event detection.
 189:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****       These RTC alternate functions can wake up the system from the Stop and 
 190:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****       Standby lowpower modes.
 191:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  [..] The system can also wake up from low power modes without depending 
 192:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****       on an external interrupt (Auto-wakeup mode), by using the RTC alarm 
 193:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****       or the RTC wakeup events.
 194:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  [..] The RTC provides a programmable time base for waking up from the 
 195:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****       Stop or Standby mode at regular intervals.
 196:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****       Wakeup from STOP and Standby modes is possible only when the RTC clock source
 197:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****       is LSE or LSI.
 198:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****   
 199:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c **** 
 200:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****           ##### Selection of RTC_AF1 alternate functions #####
 201:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  ===================================================================
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccgzaD3d.s 			page 5


 202:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  [..] The RTC_AF1 pin (PC13) can be used for the following purposes:
 203:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) AFO_ALARM output
 204:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) AFO_CALIB output
 205:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) AFI_TAMPER
 206:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    (+) AFI_TIMESTAMP
 207:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  
 208:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****  [..]   
 209:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    +-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 210:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    |     Pin         |AFO_ALARM |AFO_CALIB |AFI_TAMPER |AFI_TIMESTAMP | TAMP1INSEL |   TSINSEL    |
 211:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    |  configuration  | ENABLED  | ENABLED  |  ENABLED  |   ENABLED    |TAMPER1 pin |TIMESTAMP pin |
 212:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    |  and function   |          |          |           |              | selection  |  selection   |
 213:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    |-----------------|----------|----------|-----------|--------------|------------|--------------|
 214:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    |   Alarm out     |          |          |           |              |    Don't   |     Don't    |
 215:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    |   output OD     |     1    |Don't care|Don't care | Don't care   |    care    |     care     |
 216:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    |-----------------|----------|----------|-----------|--------------|------------|--------------|
 217:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    |   Alarm out     |          |          |           |              |    Don't   |     Don't    |
 218:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    |   output PP     |     1    |Don't care|Don't care | Don't care   |    care    |     care     |
 219:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    |-----------------|----------|----------|-----------|--------------|------------|--------------|
 220:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    | Calibration out |          |          |           |              |    Don't   |     Don't    |
 221:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    |   output PP     |     0    |    1     |Don't care | Don't care   |    care    |     care     |
 222:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    |-----------------|----------|----------|-----------|--------------|------------|--------------|
 223:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    |  TAMPER input   |          |          |           |              |            |     Don't    |
 224:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    |   floating      |     0    |    0     |     1     |      0       |      0     |     care     |
 225:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    |-----------------|----------|----------|-----------|--------------|------------|--------------|
 226:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    |  TIMESTAMP and  |          |          |           |              |            |              |
 227:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rtc.c ****    |  TAMPER input   |     0    |    0     |     1     |      1       |      0     |      0       |
